  not assert a new license for those files; see
  legacy/device-meizu-m86-cm14/UPSTREAM.md and LEGAL-NOTE.md.

- kernel/meizu/m86 is the Meizu-released m86 Linux 3.10.61 kernel source,
  based on https://github.com/meizu-m86/android_kernel_meizu_m86
  branch `cm-14.1`, commit
  `67699d9442a9557eca24ba7a489ffa1b0601e806`, licensed GPL-2.0-only.
  Android 10 donor references are pinned in docs/kernel-port.md.

- twrp/device/meizu/m86 builds against the TeamWin / Omni minimal TWRP
  manifest. Upstream revisions are pinned in docs/twrp.md:
  minimal-manifest-twrp/platform_manifest_twrp_omni `twrp-9.0` @
  `f3f57994a2aa2c92303df24bb01caff6850f7463`, TeamWin
  android_bootable_recovery `android-9.0` @
  `90e5d9559065cfa8b2b9a5dbb1c5cb7a88f034fa`.

- hardware/meizu/m86/graphics/gralloc/framebuffer.cpp is derived from
  hardware/samsung_slsi/exynos/gralloc/framebuffer.cpp at commit
  `6dce0ba9f592d75ca5747464f09669cd76c8c81e` under Apache-2.0.

- overlays/kernel-meizu-m86-case-sensitive contains byte-identical kernel
  source files from the Meizu m86 kernel commit above and remains
  GPL-2.0-only. See the COPYING file in that directory.

- patches/twrp-kernel-m86 contains kernel patches and remains GPL-2.0-only.
  See the COPYING file in that directory.

No proprietary binaries, stock firmware, or device evidence are included.
